1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:13,836
[Host] Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is October fourteenth. Japan's agriculture minister has resigned after less than a month in the job. Let's listen.

2
00:00:14,435 --> 00:00:17,315
[News] 今日のニュースです。

3
00:00:18,015 --> 00:00:26,632
[News] 農林水産大臣が、14日、高市首相に辞表を出しました。

4
00:00:27,332 --> 00:00:37,363
[News] 大臣は、先月の内閣改造で大臣になったばかりで、まだ1か月もたっていません。

5
00:00:38,064 --> 00:00:47,351
[News] 高市政権が始まってから、問題を起こして大臣が辞めるのは、初めてです。

6
00:00:48,051 --> 00:00:56,692
[News] 問題になったのは、今年5月に栃木県で開かれた会合での発言です。

7
00:00:57,392 --> 00:01:09,799
[News] 大臣は、選挙で自分を応援しなかった市と町について、「道路の予算を大きくカットした」と話していました。

8
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:19,379
[News] 先月30日、この発言の音声が、週刊誌などで報道されました。

9
00:01:20,079 --> 00:01:29,152
[News] 大臣は国会で、「予算を減らすように頼んだ事実はない」と説明しました。

10
00:01:29,852 --> 00:01:38,876
[News] しかし、地元からも「こんなことでは国が腐る」という厳しい声が出ました。

11
00:01:39,575 --> 00:01:49,319
[News] また、選挙のとき、支援者を無料のバスで送り迎えしていたことも問題になりました。

12
00:01:50,019 --> 00:02:00,243
[News] 大臣は、無料のバスを使ったことは認めましたが、法律には違反していないと話しました。

13
00:02:00,944 --> 00:02:13,039
[News] 14日、大臣は記者に、「国会の審議に、これ以上迷惑をかけるわけにはいかない」と話しました。

14
00:02:13,740 --> 00:02:20,604
[News] そして、辞めることは「自分で決めた」と説明しました。

15
00:02:21,304 --> 00:02:30,807
[News] 高市首相は辞表を受け取りましたが、大臣を選んだ首相の責任も問われています。

16
00:02:31,508 --> 00:02:33,524
[Host] Now let's break it down.

17
00:02:34,123 --> 00:02:43,364
[Slow] 農林水産大臣が、14日、高市首相に辞表を出しました。

18
00:02:44,163 --> 00:02:50,692
[Host] On the fourteenth, the agriculture minister handed a resignation letter to Prime Minister Takaichi.

19
00:02:51,292 --> 00:02:53,427
[Vocab] 辞表

20
00:02:53,828 --> 00:02:56,156
[Host] It means a letter of resignation.

21
00:02:56,756 --> 00:02:58,987
[Vocab] 首相

22
00:02:59,388 --> 00:03:01,331
[Host] It means prime minister.

23
00:03:01,931 --> 00:03:12,707
[Slow] 大臣は、先月の内閣改造で大臣になったばかりで、まだ1か月もたっていません。

24
00:03:13,508 --> 00:03:19,051
[Host] He had only just become a minister in last month's cabinet reshuffle, less than one month ago.

25
00:03:19,651 --> 00:03:22,604
[Vocab] 内閣改造

26
00:03:23,003 --> 00:03:25,283
[Host] It means a cabinet reshuffle.

27
00:03:25,883 --> 00:03:27,924
[Vocab] ばかり

28
00:03:28,324 --> 00:03:32,716
[Host] After a past verb, it means something has only just happened.

29
00:03:33,316 --> 00:03:43,252
[Slow] 高市政権が始まってから、問題を起こして大臣が辞めるのは、初めてです。

30
00:03:44,051 --> 00:03:49,068
[Host] It is the first time a minister has quit over a scandal since this government began.

31
00:03:49,668 --> 00:03:51,972
[Vocab] 政権

32
00:03:52,372 --> 00:03:54,723
[Host] It means the government in power.

33
00:03:55,324 --> 00:03:57,460
[Vocab] 辞める

34
00:03:57,860 --> 00:04:00,211
[Host] It means to quit or resign.

35
00:04:00,812 --> 00:04:10,051
[Slow] 問題になったのは、今年5月に栃木県で開かれた会合での発言です。

36
00:04:10,852 --> 00:04:14,860
[Host] The problem was something he said at a meeting in Tochigi this May.

37
00:04:15,460 --> 00:04:17,764
[Vocab] 会合

38
00:04:18,163 --> 00:04:20,492
[Host] It means a meeting or gathering.

39
00:04:21,091 --> 00:04:23,276
[Vocab] 発言

40
00:04:23,675 --> 00:04:26,172
[Host] It means a remark or statement.

41
00:04:26,771 --> 00:04:40,067
[Slow] 大臣は、選挙で自分を応援しなかった市と町について、「道路の予算を大きくカットした」と話していました。

42
00:04:40,867 --> 00:04:46,627
[Host] He said he had cut the road budget for a city and a town that did not support him in the election.

43
00:04:47,228 --> 00:04:49,387
[Vocab] 応援

44
00:04:49,788 --> 00:04:52,067
[Host] It means support or backing.

45
00:04:52,668 --> 00:04:54,803
[Vocab] 予算

46
00:04:55,204 --> 00:04:57,076
[Host] It means a budget.

47
00:04:57,675 --> 00:05:07,180
[Slow] 先月30日、この発言の音声が、週刊誌などで報道されました。

48
00:05:07,980 --> 00:05:14,771
[Host] On the thirtieth of last month, a recording of the remark was reported by weekly magazines and others.

49
00:05:15,372 --> 00:05:17,603
[Vocab] 音声

50
00:05:18,004 --> 00:05:20,764
[Host] It means audio or a voice recording.

51
00:05:21,363 --> 00:05:23,620
[Vocab] 報道

52
00:05:24,019 --> 00:05:26,012
[Host] It means news reporting.

53
00:05:26,612 --> 00:05:36,331
[Slow] 大臣は国会で、「予算を減らすように頼んだ事実はない」と説明しました。

54
00:05:37,132 --> 00:05:42,291
[Host] In the Diet, he said it was not true that he asked for the budget to be cut.

55
00:05:42,891 --> 00:05:45,124
[Vocab] 減らす

56
00:05:45,524 --> 00:05:47,396
[Host] It means to reduce.

57
00:05:47,995 --> 00:05:50,276
[Vocab] 事実

58
00:05:50,675 --> 00:05:52,548
[Host] It means a fact.

59
00:05:53,148 --> 00:06:02,819
[Slow] しかし、地元からも「こんなことでは国が腐る」という厳しい声が出ました。

60
00:06:03,620 --> 00:06:09,740
[Host] But even people in his home area spoke harshly, saying this kind of thing makes the country rot.

61
00:06:10,339 --> 00:06:12,524
[Vocab] 地元

62
00:06:12,923 --> 00:06:16,307
[Host] It means one's home area or local community.

63
00:06:16,908 --> 00:06:19,235
[Vocab] 厳しい

64
00:06:19,636 --> 00:06:21,963
[Host] It means harsh or strict.

65
00:06:22,564 --> 00:06:32,860
[Slow] また、選挙のとき、支援者を無料のバスで送り迎えしていたことも問題になりました。

66
00:06:33,660 --> 00:06:38,675
[Host] Also, giving supporters free bus rides during elections became a problem.

67
00:06:39,276 --> 00:06:41,723
[Vocab] 支援者

68
00:06:42,124 --> 00:06:43,995
[Host] It means a supporter.

69
00:06:44,596 --> 00:06:47,235
[Vocab] 送り迎え

70
00:06:47,636 --> 00:06:50,755
[Host] It means picking people up and dropping them off.

71
00:06:51,355 --> 00:07:02,324
[Slow] 大臣は、無料のバスを使ったことは認めましたが、法律には違反していないと話しました。

72
00:07:03,124 --> 00:07:07,444
[Host] He admitted using free buses, but said he did not break the law.

73
00:07:08,043 --> 00:07:10,324
[Vocab] 認める

74
00:07:10,723 --> 00:07:12,596
[Host] It means to admit.

75
00:07:13,196 --> 00:07:15,211
[Vocab] 違反

76
00:07:15,612 --> 00:07:17,483
[Host] It means a violation.

77
00:07:18,084 --> 00:07:31,043
[Slow] 14日、大臣は記者に、「国会の審議に、これ以上迷惑をかけるわけにはいかない」と話しました。

78
00:07:31,843 --> 00:07:37,843
[Host] On the fourteenth, he told reporters he could not cause any more trouble for the Diet debates.

79
00:07:38,444 --> 00:07:40,795
[Vocab] 迷惑

80
00:07:41,196 --> 00:07:44,435
[Host] It means trouble or inconvenience to others.

81
00:07:45,036 --> 00:07:47,267
[Vocab] 審議

82
00:07:47,668 --> 00:07:50,379
[Host] It means debate or deliberation.

83
00:07:50,980 --> 00:07:58,324
[Slow] そして、辞めることは「自分で決めた」と説明しました。

84
00:07:59,124 --> 00:08:01,860
[Host] And he said quitting was his own decision.

85
00:08:02,459 --> 00:08:12,660
[Slow] 高市首相は辞表を受け取りましたが、大臣を選んだ首相の責任も問われています。

86
00:08:13,459 --> 00:08:20,276
[Host] The prime minister accepted the letter, but she is also being asked about her responsibility for choosing him.

87
00:08:20,875 --> 00:08:23,180
[Vocab] 受け取る

88
00:08:23,579 --> 00:08:26,124
[Host] It means to receive or accept.

89
00:08:26,723 --> 00:08:29,028
[Vocab] 責任

90
00:08:29,427 --> 00:08:31,468
[Host] It means responsibility.

91
00:08:32,067 --> 00:08:34,827
[Host] Now listen to the full story again.

92
